//Array-branch priority pin: a string[] receiver's .length() resolves
//through the ARRAY builtin (the receiver context is the array token,
//not NK_String, so the string-builtin block declines) — the call
//measures the array (2 elements), never a string.
int main() {
    string[] words = new string[2];
    words[0] = "abc";
    return words.length();
}
